# 0010-media-prompt-reuse: image and video prompts keep and resume prompt states (prefix cache) on the Zig engine.
#
# Petabridge prototype, applied after the recipe's 0001-0009 (git apply in the TensorFold checkout's root, as
# scripts/prepare.sh applies them). Apache-2.0, as TensorFold and the recipe are.
#
# Before this patch a prompt with images or video was neither resumed nor kept (lane_host.zig's lookup gate and
# cuda_engine.zig's error.MediaPromptKept), so a multi-turn conversation with screenshots prefilled from token 0 on
# every turn. The approach follows the GLM-5.3-Flash TensorFold recipe's image prompt reuse (issue #11 of that
# recipe): kept states are keyed by the prompt's ids with each picture's content key written into its rows.
#
# What changes:
# - vision helper (Python): each picture and video frame group gets a 64-bit content key (decoded pixels' hash, the
#   pixel cap it was fitted under, its processed grid; tensorfold/vision/media_keys.py), sent as the reply header's
#   item_keys. A fixed per-image visual-token cap (TENSORFOLD_IMAGE_TOKENS_EACH, default 1024; 0 = upstream's shared
#   split) applies while images x cap fits TENSORFOLD_IMAGE_TOKENS, so an added image never refits earlier ones;
#   past that the request falls back to the shared split (served, but resumes nothing past its first image). An
#   optional host-side feature cache (TENSORFOLD_VISION_FEATURE_CACHE_MB, default 512; 0 = off) encodes each picture
#   alone and reuses its tower rows by key on later turns.
# - server: the ids the prompt cache sees are the prompt's with every picture row replaced by
#   0x80000000 | (hash(key, row) & 0x7fffffff), and row 0 tagged, so image and text states are never mixed
#   (prompt_cache.mediaKeyed, Request.cache_key); an image prompt's history length is found as the text path finds
#   it (the template's generation suffix), so its keep points are planned. "prompt_cache": false in a request
#   prefills from 0 and keeps nothing (for exactness checks).
# - engine: the MediaPromptKept refusals are gone; the media table is attached before a resume's MTP absorb (it
#   rotates through the table, as a fresh pass's absorb of that row did); keep segments carry the whole prompt's
#   media (Media.check accepts a prefix; the table is cut to the segment; a following rank's row count may pass the
#   segment); TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_DIGEST also prints the sliced fill's chunk digests.
#
# Prototype: host-side tests only (zig build test, zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh, tests/test_media_prompt_reuse.py);
# not yet run on GPUs. See the Petabridge image README for the exactness test plan.

